   "notes": "15-16 Bridge Street: 16th-century jettied timber-framed house, dark exposed studs and braces on white infill, two jetties; three grey-framed projecting oriel windows on the first floor, four casements under the eaves on the second, steep old-tile roof. Ground floor: dark timber shopfront with carriage passage (16a) at left and a cyan cafe front at right. Commons '15 and 16 Bridge Street, Cambridge.jpg'. Positions scaled from the photo to the 7.8 m wall."
